## 1. Verified Core Literature (12 Papers)

### 1. Vanni et al. (2022) — The AGNOSTOS Framework
* **Title:** Unifying the known and unknown microbial coding sequence space
* **Authors / Year:** Chiara Vanni, Matthew S. Schechter, Silvia G. Acinas, Albert Barberán, Pier Luigi Buttigieg, Emilio O. Casamayor, Tom O. Delmont, Carlos M. Duarte, A. Murat Eren, Robert D. Finn, Renzo Kottmann, Alex Mitchell, Pablo Sánchez, Kimmo Siren, Martin Steinegger, Frank Oliver Glöckner, Antonio Fernández-Guerra (2022)
* **DOI:** [`10.7554/eLife.67667`](https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.67667)
* **Publisher URL:** [https://elifesciences.org/articles/67667](https://elifesciences.org/articles/67667)
* **Accessible Full-Text:** [`Vanni_2022_AGNOSTOS_eLife_preprint.pdf`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/01_dark_catalogues/Vanni_2022_AGNOSTOS_eLife_preprint.pdf) (5.2 MB) & [`Vanni_2022_AGNOSTOS_fulltext.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/01_dark_catalogues/Vanni_2022_AGNOSTOS_fulltext.xml) (253 KB)
* **Status in `references.bib`:** Already cited (`vanni2022agnostos`).
* **Precise Claim & Limitation for P4:** Introduced the AGNOSTOS framework partitioning coding space into Knowns with/without Pfam, Genomic Unknowns (GUs), and Environmental Unknowns (EUs). Documented that ~30% of microbial genes are unknown and lineage-restricted.  
  *Limitation:* **>80% of environmental unknown gene clusters could not be placed into MAGs**, leaving them unbinned. P4 resolves this by requiring genome-resolved placement on HQ+MQ binned contigs and verifying persistence across 5 field expeditions.

