### 2. Rodríguez del Río et al. (2024) — FESNov
* **Title:** Functional and evolutionary significance of unknown genes from uncultivated taxa
* **Authors / Year:** Álvaro Rodríguez del Río, Joaquín Giner-Lamia, Carlos P. Cantalapiedra, Jorge Botas, Ziqi Deng, Ana Hernández-Plaza, Martí Munar-Palmer, Saray Santamaría-Hernando, José J. Rodríguez-Herva, Hans-Joachim Ruscheweyh, Lucas Paoli, Thomas S. B. Schmidt, Shinichi Sunagawa, Peer Bork, Emilia López-Solanilla, Luis Pedro Coelho, Jaime Huerta-Cepas (2024)
* **DOI:** [`10.1038/s41586-023-06955-z`](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06955-z)
* **Publisher URL:** [https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06955-z](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06955-z)
* **Accessible Full-Text:** [`RodriguezdelRio_2024_FESNov_Nature.pdf`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/01_dark_catalogues/RodriguezdelRio_2024_FESNov_Nature.pdf) (4.9 MB) & [`RodriguezdelRio_2024_FESNov_fulltext.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/01_dark_catalogues/RodriguezdelRio_2024_FESNov_fulltext.xml) (116 KB)
* **Status in `references.bib`:** Already cited (`rodriguezdelrio2024fesnov`).
* **Precise Claim & Limitation for P4:** Curated 404,085 FESNov gene families exclusive to uncultivated taxa, showing purifying selection ($dN/dS < 1$) and framing unknown genes as clade-defining synapomorphic markers of uncultivated phyla (CPR, etc.).  
  *Limitation:* Operates on cross-sectional pooled genomes. P4 shows that in extreme hyperarid soils, dark families are overwhelmingly carried by ordinary, dominant named phyla (Actinomycetota 32%, Thermoplasmatota 19%) as **strain-variable accessory content** (only 16% shared between cultured strains and MAGs of the identical species) rather than lineage-defining core markers.

